      "title": "User delete route missing admin check",
      "description": "The DELETE /users/:id route does not run requireAdmin, unlike its sibling admin routes. Any caller who reaches the server can delete any user by id. A non-admin user can delete other user accounts. This causes data loss and breaks access control. Add requireAdmin as middleware on the DELETE /users/:id route.",
      "suggested_change": "admin.delete(\"/users/:id\", requireAdmin, async (req, res) => {",
      "source": "lens:id-enumeration-sequential",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The DELETE /users/:id route does not run requireAdmin, unlike its sibling admin routes. Any caller who reaches the server can delete any user by id.",
      "consequence": "A non-admin user can delete other user accounts. This causes data loss and breaks access control.",
      "fix": "Add requireAdmin as middleware on the DELETE /users/:id route."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "file_path": "src/admin.js",
      "line_number": 22,
      "line_end": 25,
      "title": "Purge deletes run as unhandled floating promises",
      "description": "The forEach callback starts each async removeUser call, but nothing awaits or catches the returned promises. The handler sends the removed count before any delete finishes. removeUser throws for an unknown id, and the unhandled rejection crashes the Node process. The response reports every id as removed even when a delete fails. Await Promise.all over ids.map with removeUser, or Promise.allSettled to count successes. Respond only after the deletes settle.",
      "suggested_change": "  await Promise.all(ids.map((id) => db.removeUser(id)));\n  res.json({ removed: ids.length });",
      "source": "lens:async-floating-promise",
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The forEach callback starts each async removeUser call, but nothing awaits or catches the returned promises. The handler sends the removed count before any delete finishes.",
      "consequence": "removeUser throws for an unknown id, and the unhandled rejection crashes the Node process. The response reports every id as removed even when a delete fails.",
      "fix": "Await Promise.all over ids.map with removeUser, or Promise.allSettled to count successes. Respond only after the deletes settle."
    },
